# el-openglo.magic — signatures for the artifact kinds stock file(1) calls text/plain.
#
# ⚑ MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED.  Stock file-5.46 identifies this repo's SVG and Python
# correctly and returns text/plain for QML, .colors and .bib — three of five
# artifact kinds. Each signature below closes a gap that was observed, not one
# that was imagined.
#
# ⚑ SEARCH, NOT OFFSET 0.  Every one of these begins with something other than
# its identifying token: QML files open with a `//` comment, .bib with a long
# prose header, .colors with a [ColorEffects:...] group that is not first in
# every variant. An `0 string` anchor matched NONE of them; `search/<n>` does,
# and the window has to be wide enough — .bib needed 8192 because the warrants
# files carry several hundred bytes of commentary before the first @misc{.
#
# ⚑ AND THIS FILE AUGMENTS, IT DOES NOT REPLACE.  `file --magic-file X` uses X
# ALONE: SVG and Python silently regress to text/plain. The caller must
# colon-append the system database, which scripts/identify.py does.

# QML — the dominant artifact kind here (Plasma widgets, the SegmentChar substrate)
0	search/512	import\ QtQuick	QML source
!:mime	text/x-qml

# KDE colour scheme — the emitted .colors files, one per variant
0	search/256	[ColorEffects:	KDE color scheme
!:mime	text/x-kde-colorscheme

# BibTeX — the paperkit warrants that carry this repo's claim graph
0	search/8192	@misc{	BibTeX warrants
!:mime	text/x-bibtex

# Konsole scheme — the terminal counterpart of .colors
0	search/256	[Background]	Konsole color scheme
!:mime	text/x-konsole-colorscheme
